      "Language": "cze",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Findings in a 56-year old man who died 3 months after laser heart surgery were described. In the site of surgery (anterior and lateral wall of left heart ventricle) patent slit-like channels we found that may or may not have been performed by laser. Channels were indistinguishable from lymphatics. In second case, a 59-year old woman died 5-days after laser revascularization. Channels filled by fibrin, cellular debris and polymorphonuclear leukocytes were found, none of them patent."},
